window.ORBIT_DOC_PAGES = {"index.html": {"title": "Orbit — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"orbit\">Orbit</h1>\n<div class=\"hero\">\n<img src=\"../logos/orbit.png\" alt=\"Orbit logo\">\n<div>\n<p class=\"kicker\">Documentation · Orbit for Windows</p>\n<p class=\"name\">All your creative tools, in one app</p>\n<p class=\"tag\">Download, convert, enhance and create: video, audio, image and 3D, with AI tools that run on\nyour own computer.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"badges\">\n<span>Windows 10 and 11</span>\n<span>17 tools</span>\n<span>Local AI (GPU)</span>\n<span>English, Français, Español, Deutsch, Italiano, Português</span>\n</div>\n\n<h2 id=\"what-orbit-does\">What Orbit does</h2>\n<p>Orbit brings into one window tools you would usually find in a dozen programs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>download</strong> videos, playlists and music from hundreds of sites (YouTube, TikTok, Twitch, Spotify, Deezer,\n  file hosts…) and follow your favourite channels;</li>\n<li><strong>convert</strong> almost any file: video (accelerated by NVIDIA graphics cards), audio, image, LUT, fonts, 3D\n  models, documents, After Effects presets;</li>\n<li><strong>enhance and create with AI</strong>: generate images, erase or replace an object, remove a background, upscale a\n  video, make it smoother, turn an image into a 3D model, retouch a video shot;</li>\n<li><strong>work on sound</strong>: split vocals from music, denoise, normalize, transcribe and subtitle;</li>\n<li><strong>organize and share</strong>: media library, a toolbox of more than 60 small tools, encrypted cloud storage.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Most AI tools run <strong>on your computer</strong>: your files never leave your machine, and once the models are\ndownloaded, they work offline.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/home.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Orbit home screen: every tool, sorted by category\" src=\"images/home.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Orbit home screen: every tool, sorted by category</figcaption></figure>\n<p class=\"gallery g3\"><img src=\"../showcase/cite-flottante.jpg\" alt=\"Made with AI Generation: a floating city\"><img src=\"../showcase/robot-cafe.jpg\" alt=\"Made with AI Generation: a robot in a retro café\"><img src=\"../showcase/montagne.jpg\" alt=\"Made with AI Generation: a mountain as a vector illustration\"></p>\n\n<h2 id=\"contents\">Contents</h2>\n<div class=\"cards\">\n<a href=\"installation.html\">Installation<small>Install Orbit, first launch, updates.</small></a>\n<a href=\"interface.html\">The interface<small>Home, search, menu, AI assistant.</small></a>\n<a href=\"telechargements.html\">Downloads<small>Videos, music, playlists, subscriptions.</small></a>\n<a href=\"conversion.html\">Conversion<small>Universal converter and HandBrake.</small></a>\n<a href=\"ia-image.html\">AI for images<small>Generation, magic eraser, cutout, enhance.</small></a>\n<a href=\"ia-video-3d.html\">AI for video and 3D<small>Interpolation, Topaz, Paint a plate, 3D creation.</small></a>\n<a href=\"audio-transcription.html\">Audio and transcription<small>Audio Studio, automatic subtitles.</small></a>\n<a href=\"boite-a-outils.html\">Toolbox and media library<small>More than 60 quick tools, your media.</small></a>\n<a href=\"drive.html\">Discord Drive<small>Encrypted storage and sharing by code.</small></a>\n<a href=\"reglages.html\">Settings<small>Every settings page, graphics card.</small></a>\n<a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium<small>What is included and how to activate it.</small></a>\n<a href=\"depannage.html\">Troubleshooting<small>Common problems and their fixes.</small></a>\n</div>\n\n<h2 id=\"what-you-need\">What you need</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Minimum</th>\n<th>For the AI tools</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>System</td>\n<td>Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit</td>\n<td>Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Memory</td>\n<td>8 GB</td>\n<td>16 GB or more</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Graphics card</td>\n<td>Any recent card</td>\n<td>NVIDIA RTX, 8 GB of video memory or more (16 GB for 3D and Paint a plate)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Disk</td>\n<td>1 GB for the app</td>\n<td>From a few GB to more than 60 GB depending on the AI models installed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Internet</td>\n<td>To download, and for the first install of the models</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Download, conversion and toolbox features work on any PC. The AI tools use the graphics card when there is one;\nsome (AI 3D Creation, Paint a plate, local AI Generation) need an <strong>NVIDIA</strong> card.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"next\" href=\"installation.html\"><span>Next</span>Installation</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#what-orbit-does\">What Orbit does</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#contents\">Contents</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#what-you-need\">What you need</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../index.html"}, "installation.html": {"title": "Installation — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"installation\">Installation</h1>\n<h2 id=\"install-orbit\">Install Orbit</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Download the installer: the <strong>Download Orbit</strong> button at the top left of this page, or the\n   <a href=\"https://github.com/ThomasDM40-dev/orbit-releases/releases/latest\">Orbit releases page</a> (file\n   <code>Orbit-Installer.exe</code>).</li>\n<li>Run <code>Orbit-Installer.exe</code> and follow the install window.</li>\n<li>At the end, click the launch button: Orbit opens.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Orbit installs for your Windows account only (no administrator rights needed) and creates an <strong>Orbit</strong>\nshortcut on the desktop and in the Start menu.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If Windows shows \"Windows protected your PC\", click <strong>More info</strong> then <strong>Run anyway</strong>. This message appears for\nrecent apps that Windows does not know yet.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"first-launch\">First launch</h2>\n<p>On first launch, Orbit asks what you do (video editor, motion design, 3D, audio, downloading, image\ncreation…). It then shows only the tools you need; <strong>I want to explore everything</strong> keeps them all. At the\nbottom, you also pick the theme and the accent color.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/onboarding.jpg\"><img alt=\"The setup wizard: pick what you do, Orbit arranges its tools\" src=\"images/onboarding.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The setup wizard: pick what you do, Orbit arranges its tools</figcaption></figure>\n<p>You can run this wizard again at any time: <strong>Settings › Appearance › Setup wizard › Relaunch</strong>. Hidden tabs stay\nreachable through search (<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd>) and the <strong>Menu</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"modules-installed-on-demand\">Modules installed on demand</h2>\n<p>Orbit stays light: heavy engines are only downloaded the first time you need them (ffmpeg, yt-dlp, AI engines,\nmodels). Each tool shows an <strong>Install</strong> button when something is missing, with a progress bar. The <strong>Settings ›\nModules &amp; AI</strong> page lists every module, its size and its state, and installs or updates them in one go.</p>\n<p>Modules and models live in the <code>.orbit</code> folder of your user folder (<code>C:\\Users\\&lt;you&gt;\\.orbit</code>). <strong>Settings ›\nSystem › Orbit data folder › Open</strong> shows it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"updates\">Updates</h2>\n<p>Orbit updates itself: at launch, it checks for a new version, downloads it in the background and installs it\nat the next restart. After an update, a window presents what is new.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>To check by hand: <strong>Settings › About › Check for updates</strong>.</li>\n<li>The download engine (yt-dlp) also updates itself at every launch, to keep up with site changes.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If a version is too old, the AI tools show <strong>Update required</strong> with a button that installs the latest version.</p>\n<h2 id=\"uninstall\">Uninstall</h2>\n<p><strong>Windows Settings › Apps › Installed apps</strong>, find <strong>Orbit</strong>, then <strong>Uninstall</strong>. The <code>.orbit</code> folder\n(modules, AI models, settings) is not removed: delete it by hand to get the disk space back.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"index.html\"><span>Previous</span>Orbit</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"interface.html\"><span>Next</span>The interface</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#install-orbit\">Install Orbit</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#first-launch\">First launch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#modules-installed-on-demand\">Modules installed on demand</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#updates\">Updates</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#uninstall\">Uninstall</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../installation.html"}, "interface.html": {"title": "The interface — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"the-interface\">The interface</h1>\n<h2 id=\"home\">Home</h2>\n<p>The home screen shows every tool, sorted into five categories: <strong>Download</strong>, <strong>Conversion</strong>, <strong>Creative AI</strong>,\n<strong>Studio &amp; Tools</strong> and <strong>Cloud</strong>. The <strong>Trending</strong> and <strong>New</strong> rows highlight the most used and the latest\ntools. Click a card to open the tool.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/home.jpg\"><img alt=\"The home screen\" src=\"images/home.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The home screen</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The <strong>sidebar</strong> on the left stays visible everywhere: it lists the tools by category, with <strong>Premium</strong> (your\nlicence state) and <strong>Settings</strong> at the bottom. In a small window it folds away: the menu button at the top left\nopens it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"search-ctrlk\">Search (Ctrl+K)</h2>\n<p>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd> anywhere, or click the search box at the top: type a few letters, then\n<kbd>Enter</kbd> to open the tool. Search also finds the tools you have hidden.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/search.jpg\"><img alt=\"Quick search\" src=\"images/search.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Quick search</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"the-menu\">The Menu</h2>\n<p>The <strong>Menu</strong> button, at the top right, groups the general commands:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>File</strong>: Premium, Settings, <strong>Import</strong> (a list of links), open the download folder, Quit;</li>\n<li><strong>Downloads</strong>: pause all, resume all, restart failed downloads, clear finished ones, cancel all;</li>\n<li><strong>Language</strong>: English, French, Spanish, German, Italian, Portuguese;</li>\n<li><strong>Tools</strong>: open the Orbit folder, reinstall or update yt-dlp, changelog, back up and restore subscriptions,\n  AI Assistant;</li>\n<li>tab visibility: tick or untick the tools to show in the sidebar.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure><a href=\"images/menu.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Menu\" src=\"images/menu.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Menu</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Next to it, the speaker icon mutes or restores the small interface sounds.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-ai-assistant\">The AI assistant</h2>\n<p>The round button at the bottom right opens <strong>Orbit AI</strong>, an assistant that knows the app. Ask it what you want\nto do (\"compress this video for Discord\", \"where do I set the quality?\"): it answers, opens the right tool or\nchanges a setting for you. You can also drop a file on it.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/assistant.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Orbit AI assistant\" src=\"images/assistant.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Orbit AI assistant</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The assistant uses a free local AI (about 2 GB, downloaded once, works offline) or, if you add your own key,\nAnthropic's Claude: <strong>Settings › AI &amp; Performance › AI Assistant</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"task-center\">Task center</h2>\n<p>Long jobs (conversions, AI renders, encodes) show up in the <strong>task center</strong> with their progress, even when you\nswitch tabs. AI tools that use the graphics card run one at a time: a waiting job shows <strong>Waiting for a GPU\nslot…</strong> (set in <strong>Settings › Downloads › Simultaneous AI jobs (GPU)</strong>).</p>\n<h2 id=\"drag-and-drop\">Drag and drop</h2>\n<p>Almost every tool accepts files dragged from Windows Explorer, one at a time or many at once. You can also add\n<strong>Orbit</strong> to Explorer's right-click menu (<strong>Settings › Downloads › Windows right-click menu</strong>) to compress or\ncrop a file without opening the app.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"installation.html\"><span>Previous</span>Installation</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"telechargements.html\"><span>Next</span>Downloads</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#home\">Home</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#search-ctrlk\">Search (Ctrl+K)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#the-menu\">The Menu</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#the-ai-assistant\">The AI assistant</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#task-center\">Task center</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#drag-and-drop\">Drag and drop</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../interface.html"}, "telechargements.html": {"title": "Downloads — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"downloads\">Downloads</h1>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Only download content you have the right to copy: your own videos, royalty-free content, or for a use allowed\nby the law of your country.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"download-a-video\">Download a video</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Copy the link of the video (YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, X, Vimeo, Twitch, SoundCloud… several hundred sites\n   are supported).</li>\n<li>In the <strong>Downloads</strong> tab, paste it in the top bar (clipboard button on the left, or\n   <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>V</kbd>). Orbit analyzes the link and shows the title and thumbnail.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Download</strong> to start right away, or press <kbd>Enter</kbd> to <strong>queue</strong> it and start everything later\n   with <strong>Download all</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure><a href=\"images/downloads.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Downloads tab with finished, queued and failed items\" src=\"images/downloads.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Downloads tab with finished, queued and failed items</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Files go to the folder shown at the top right (<strong>Downloads</strong> by default); click it to change it. Each item can\nalso have its own folder (folder icon on its row).</p>\n<h2 id=\"quality-and-format\">Quality and format</h2>\n<p>The <strong>Highest Quality</strong> button, on the right of the bar, opens the format choice:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Download Audio Only?</strong>: a switch to keep only the sound (MP3, FLAC, WAV, M4A, OGG);</li>\n<li><strong>Download Format</strong>: from <strong>Highest Quality Video and Audio</strong> to 8K, 4K, 2K, 1080p, 720p, 480p, 360p, 144p, or\n  standard MP4;</li>\n<li><strong>Thumbnail</strong>: <strong>Off</strong>, <strong>Separate image</strong>, <strong>Embedded in the video</strong> or <strong>Both</strong>, with the image format (JPG,\n  PNG, WEBP) and size.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This choice applies to the next links. For a queued item, the drop-down list on its row changes its own format.</p>\n<p>The icons of the bar turn on options for the next links:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Icon</th>\n<th>Effect</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SNIFFER</strong></td>\n<td>opens the built-in browser to catch hidden videos on a page (see below)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Document</td>\n<td>imports a playlist exported as CSV (Exportify, TuneMyMusic, Soundiiz)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Image</td>\n<td>thumbnail (set in the quality menu)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>List</td>\n<td>downloads the whole playlist instead of one video</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>CC</td>\n<td>embeds subtitles in the file</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cookie</td>\n<td>uses your browser's cookies (Chrome) for content that needs a login</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Permanent settings (H.264 forced for editing, metadata, chapters, SponsorBlock, automatic subtitles…) are in\n<strong>Settings › Downloads</strong>, see <a href=\"reglages.html#downloads\">Settings</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-download-list\">The download list</h2>\n<p>Each row shows the source, the state, then the resolution, codecs, duration, size and container once the file\nis ready. The buttons on the right depend on the state:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Queued</strong>: pick the format, the folder, <strong>Download</strong>, or <strong>…</strong> for <strong>Advanced options (Trimmer /\n  Scheduler)</strong>:<ul>\n<li><strong>Trimmer</strong>: keep only a part (start and end, for example <code>01:20</code> and <code>02:45</code>);</li>\n<li><strong>Scheduler</strong>: start the download at a set time.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Active</strong>: pause, resume, cancel; the row shows the speed and the time left.</li>\n<li><strong>Done</strong>: <strong>Play in Orbit</strong> (built-in player), open the folder, remove from the list.</li>\n<li><strong>File deleted</strong>: the file is no longer on disk; <strong>Download again</strong> gets it back.</li>\n<li><strong>Failed — see logs</strong>: the log explains the error; <strong>Retry</strong> starts again.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>At the top of the list: the counters (<strong>Queued</strong>, <strong>Done</strong>, <strong>Failed</strong>), sorting (<strong>Date</strong>, <strong>Name</strong>,\n<strong>Size</strong>), three views (grid, list, compact) and <strong>Clear</strong> to remove finished items.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If Orbit or Windows closes during a download, Orbit resumes it at the next launch where it stopped.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"music-spotify-deezer-and-csv\">Music: Spotify, Deezer and CSV</h2>\n<p>Paste a <strong>Spotify</strong> link (track, album, playlist or artist) or a <strong>Deezer</strong> link in the same bar. Orbit reads\nthe track list, finds each song on YouTube Music and saves it with its title, artist, album and cover (and\nsynced <code>.lrc</code> lyrics when they exist).</p>\n<p>Spotify only shows the first 100 tracks of a playlist. For a longer playlist, export it as CSV (with Exportify,\nTuneMyMusic or Soundiiz) then import the file with the <strong>Document</strong> icon of the bar.</p>\n<p>Orbit bypasses no protection: the sound comes from the public versions found on YouTube Music, not from\nSpotify.</p>\n<h2 id=\"twitch\">Twitch</h2>\n<p>Twitch <strong>VODs</strong> and <strong>clips</strong> download by pasting their link. For a subscriber-only VOD, first sign in to your\nTwitch account in the built-in browser (<strong>SNIFFER</strong>): Orbit reuses that session.</p>\n<h2 id=\"file-hosts\">File hosts</h2>\n<p>File host links (1fichier, MediaFire, Pixeldrain, Gofile…) also go in the bar. Orbit opens the page in the\nbackground, clicks the free download button, waits for the countdown if there is one, then downloads over\n<strong>several connections</strong> when the site allows it (often much faster than a browser). If a captcha shows up, the\nwindow appears so you can solve it.</p>\n<p>Limits set by a free site (waiting, capped speed) stay those of the site: Orbit does not bypass them.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-built-in-browser-sniffer\">The built-in browser (Sniffer)</h2>\n<p>Some pages hide their video (embedded players, sites that need a login). Click <strong>SNIFFER</strong>: a browser opens\ninside Orbit. Go to the page and play the video: Orbit detects the streams and offers to download them.\nStreams in pieces (HLS, DASH) are rebuilt into one file.</p>\n<h2 id=\"subscriptions\">Subscriptions</h2>\n<p>The <strong>Subscriptions</strong> tab follows channels or playlists and downloads new videos on its own.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Paste the address of a channel or a playlist (for example <code>youtube.com/@creator</code>).</li>\n<li>Pick <strong>Video</strong> or <strong>Audio (MP3)</strong>, then <strong>Subscribe</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure><a href=\"images/subscriptions.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Subscriptions tab\" src=\"images/subscriptions.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Subscriptions tab</figcaption></figure>\n<p>For each subscription, set the <strong>Quality</strong>, the <strong>Number of videos</strong> (the latest N or <strong>All</strong>) and <strong>No Shorts\nor lives</strong>. At the top, the check interval sets how often Orbit looks for new videos, and <strong>Check all</strong> checks\nright now. Each subscription can be paused, checked alone or removed.</p>\n<p>To keep your subscriptions when you change PC: <strong>Menu › Tools › Export/Backup Subscriptions</strong>, then\n<strong>Import/Restore Subscriptions</strong> on the other PC.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"interface.html\"><span>Previous</span>The interface</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"conversion.html\"><span>Next</span>Conversion</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#download-a-video\">Download a video</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#quality-and-format\">Quality and format</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#the-download-list\">The download list</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#music-spotify-deezer-and-csv\">Music: Spotify, Deezer and CSV</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#twitch\">Twitch</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#file-hosts\">File hosts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#the-built-in-browser-sniffer\">The built-in browser (Sniffer)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#subscriptions\">Subscriptions</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../telechargements.html"}, "conversion.html": {"title": "Conversion — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"conversion\">Conversion</h1>\n<h2 id=\"the-converter\">The Converter</h2>\n<p>The <strong>Converter</strong> turns almost any kind of file into another. Drop files or <strong>whole folders</strong> (Orbit goes\nthrough subfolders) in the area, or click the files or folder button. Orbit recognizes each file and offers the\npossible output formats.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/convertpro.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Converter, ready for files\" src=\"images/convertpro.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Converter, ready for files</figcaption></figure>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Category</th>\n<th>Input</th>\n<th>Output</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Video</td>\n<td>MP4, MKV, MOV, AVI, WEBM…</td>\n<td>MP4, MOV, ProRes, MKV, WEBM, AVI, GIF, or audio extraction (MP3, WAV, FLAC, M4A)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Audio</td>\n<td>MP3, WAV, FLAC, M4A, OGG…</td>\n<td>WAV, MP3, FLAC, AAC, OGG, OPUS, M4A, with tag editing (title, artist, album, year, cover)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Image</td>\n<td>JPG, PNG, WEBP, HEIC, TIFF, BMP…</td>\n<td>PNG, JPG, WEBP, AVIF, TIFF, BMP</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>LUT</td>\n<td><code>.cube</code>, <code>.3dl</code></td>\n<td><code>.cube</code> ↔ <code>.3dl</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fonts</td>\n<td>TTF, OTF</td>\n<td>TTF, WOFF, WOFF2</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3D</td>\n<td>FBX, OBJ, GLB, GLTF, STL, PLY, DAE…</td>\n<td>GLB, OBJ, STL, PLY</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Documents</td>\n<td>DOCX, XLSX, Markdown</td>\n<td>PDF, HTML</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>After Effects</td>\n<td><code>.ffx</code>, <code>.aep</code></td>\n<td>analysis (effects and required plugins) and After Effects version change</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"video-settings\">Video settings</h3>\n<p>Select a video file to see its settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Encoder</strong>: <strong>Auto (GPU if available)</strong>, <strong>NVIDIA GPU (NVENC)</strong> (much faster) or <strong>Processor (CPU)</strong> (slightly\n  smaller files). If the GPU fails, Orbit retries on the processor by itself.</li>\n<li><strong>Codec</strong>: H.264 (works everywhere), H.265, AV1, or <strong>fast copy</strong> (no re-encoding, instant, when the output\n  format allows it).</li>\n<li><strong>Quality</strong>: high, balanced or small, and a <strong>maximum height</strong> (1080p, 720p…).</li>\n<li><strong>Target size</strong>: to stay under an upload limit: <strong>Discord (10 MB)</strong>, <strong>WhatsApp (16 MB)</strong>, <strong>E-mail (25 MB)</strong>,\n  <strong>Discord Nitro (50 MB)</strong>, <strong>Nitro+ (500 MB)</strong> or a custom size.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Every audio track and the subtitles are kept when the container accepts them. If a track cannot be kept (for\nexample image subtitles in an MP4), the row says so in orange.</p>\n<h3 id=\"the-queue\">The queue</h3>\n<p>Drag a row by its handle to change the order: the queue always takes the first waiting row, even if you\nreorder it during the conversion. With the graphics card, two videos are converted at the same time.</p>\n<h3 id=\"after-effects\">After Effects</h3>\n<p>For a <code>.ffx</code> preset or a <code>.aep</code> project, Orbit lists the effects used and the <strong>third-party plugins required</strong>.\nIt can also change the After Effects version of a file so it opens in an older or newer version, and, if After\nEffects is installed on your PC, use it to save a project in another version or apply a preset to a\ncomposition.</p>\n<h2 id=\"handbrake\">HandBrake</h2>\n<p>The <strong>HandBrake</strong> tab drives the well-known encoder for advanced compression. The first time, click <strong>Install\nHandBrake</strong> (automatic download).</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/handbrake.jpg\"><img alt=\"The HandBrake tab\" src=\"images/handbrake.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The HandBrake tab</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li>Drop your videos in the area (several at once).</li>\n<li>Select a file to set its encoding, or set it once and apply it to the whole queue.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Encode queue</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The settings, by section:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Preset &amp; Format</strong>: an official HandBrake preset as a base, or <strong>None (manual settings)</strong>; container; <strong>Web\n  optimized (progressive playback)</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Video</strong>: encoder, encoding speed, <strong>Constant quality (RF)</strong> (lower = better) or <strong>Average bitrate</strong> with\n  <strong>2-pass</strong>; maximum resolution; frames per second; rotation. The estimated size is shown.</li>\n<li><strong>Filters</strong>: denoise (NLMeans), sharpen (Lapsharp), deinterlace, deblock, black and white.</li>\n<li><strong>Audio &amp; Output</strong>: <strong>Copy (no re-encoding)</strong> or audio bitrate; <strong>Keep subtitles</strong>; output folder.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Save your settings as a personal preset to find them later.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"telechargements.html\"><span>Previous</span>Downloads</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"ia-image.html\"><span>Next</span>AI for images</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#the-converter\">The Converter</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#handbrake\">HandBrake</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../conversion.html"}, "ia-image.html": {"title": "AI for images — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"ai-for-images\">AI for images</h1>\n<p>These four tools are part of <a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium</a>. They run on your computer; the models download the\nfirst time you need them.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ai-generation\">AI Generation</h2>\n<p>Describe an image, Orbit creates it.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/imagegen.jpg\"><img alt=\"AI Generation: the description on the left, your creations on the right\" src=\"images/imagegen.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>AI Generation: the description on the left, your creations on the right</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li>Write the <strong>Description (prompt)</strong>: what you want to see, the style, the light. <strong>Auto prompt enhancement</strong>\n   fills out a short description.</li>\n<li>Pick a <strong>Style</strong>: None, Photorealistic, Cinematic, 3D / Blender, Anime, Digital Art, Watercolor, Cyberpunk,\n   Minimalist, Logo / Vector.</li>\n<li>Pick the <strong>AI model</strong>:<ul>\n<li><strong>Orbit Local — FLUX Klein on your GPU</strong>: the best understanding of descriptions, can write legible text;\n needs an NVIDIA card and the engine installed by <a href=\"ia-video-3d.html#paint-a-plate\">Paint a plate</a>;</li>\n<li><strong>Orbit Local — SDXL on your GPU</strong>: NVIDIA card, about 7 GB to download the first time;</li>\n<li><strong>Flux</strong> (free online service): for PCs without an NVIDIA card; adds a watermark and limits the size, about\n one image every 45 seconds.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Set the <strong>Format / Ratio</strong> (1:1, 16:9, 9:16, 4:3, 3:4, 3:2, 21:9), the <strong>Number of images</strong> (1 to 4) and the\n   <strong>Seed</strong>: a fixed seed gives the same image again, handy to tune a description word by word.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Generate the image</strong> (or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>Enter</kbd>). With the local engines, the image shows up\n   and sharpens live while it is computed.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Each image of the gallery has its buttons: open, open the folder, <strong>Reuse prompt + seed</strong>, copy the prompt, see\nthe logs, delete. Adding to the queue chains several descriptions.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ai-magic-eraser\">AI Magic Eraser</h2>\n<p>Erase an object from a photo, or replace it with something else, like Photoshop's generative fill.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/inpaint.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Magic Eraser: tools on the left, photo in the middle\" src=\"images/inpaint.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Magic Eraser: tools on the left, photo in the middle</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li>Drop a photo in the area (JPG, PNG, WEBP, TIFF, AVIF…).</li>\n<li>Select the area to change:<ul>\n<li><strong>AI selection (click the object)</strong>: click an object, its outline is found for you; click again to grow\n it, <kbd>Shift</kbd>+click or right-click to remove a part;</li>\n<li><strong>Detect objects</strong> offers every object found in the photo;</li>\n<li><strong>Brush</strong> and <strong>Eraser</strong> to paint or fix the area by hand.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>In the prompt field (optional):<ul>\n<li>leave it empty and click <strong>🧽 Erase</strong>: the object disappears, the background is rebuilt;</li>\n<li>describe what to put instead (\"a leather backpack\", \"a tree\") and click <strong>✨ Generate / Replace</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>The result is saved in the <strong>Output folder</strong>; <strong>Undo the last removal</strong> goes back.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The <strong>Engine</strong> is chosen above the tools:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>FLUX Klein</strong>: understands the whole scene, works on the full image up to 1920 pixels; NVIDIA card and the\n  <a href=\"ia-video-3d.html#paint-a-plate\">Paint a plate</a> engine. Used to replace (erasing always goes through LaMa, which\n  is more reliable);</li>\n<li><strong>Standard</strong>: LaMa to erase, Stable Diffusion to generate, with three levels: <strong>Fast</strong> (modest PC),\n  <strong>Quality</strong> (powerful PC) and <strong>SDXL HQ</strong> (NVIDIA card, about 6.5 GB the first time).</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>To replace a background, select the <strong>background</strong>, not the person: only the selected area changes.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"ai-cutout\">AI Cutout</h2>\n<p>Removes the background of a video, without a green screen.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/matting.jpg\"><img alt=\"AI Cutout\" src=\"images/matting.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>AI Cutout</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li>Drop one or more videos.</li>\n<li>Select a file and set:<ul>\n<li><strong>Model &amp; quality</strong>: <strong>Fast (512p)</strong>, <strong>Balanced (960p)</strong> or <strong>Max (source)</strong>;</li>\n<li><strong>Background</strong>: transparent (<strong>WebM VP9</strong>, <strong>ProRes 4444</strong> or <strong>PNG sequence</strong>, ready for After Effects and\n Premiere), a background color, a blur or a background image;</li>\n<li><strong>Edge refinement</strong>: soften the edges, shrink or grow the mask to remove a fringe.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Preview (3s)</strong> shows the result over 3 seconds (the checkerboard = transparent areas).</li>\n<li><strong>Cut out</strong>, or <strong>Apply to the whole queue</strong> then <strong>Run queue</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"ai-enhance\">AI Enhance</h2>\n<p>Upscales, cleans and stabilizes your videos and images.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/enhance.jpg\"><img alt=\"AI Enhance\" src=\"images/enhance.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>AI Enhance</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Three tabs: <strong>Queue &amp; Settings</strong>, <strong>Before/After Preview</strong> (compare a frame before you start) and <strong>GPU\nPerformance</strong> (live load and memory of the card).</p>\n<p>The settings, by section:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI Upscale (Real-ESRGAN)</strong>: model, scale or target resolution, tile size (smaller if the card has little\n  memory), <strong>TTA</strong> mode (best quality, slower);</li>\n<li><strong>Video restoration</strong>: denoise (classic and temporal), compression recovery, anti-banding, detail recovery,\n  deinterlace, brightness, contrast, saturation, gamma;</li>\n<li><strong>Stabilization</strong> in two passes, with smoothing, sensitivity and auto zoom to hide the edges;</li>\n<li><strong>Frame interpolation (RIFE)</strong>: output frames per second or slow motion;</li>\n<li><strong>Sharpening &amp; Export</strong>: artifact-free sharpening, format and codec.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Save your settings as a preset, then <strong>Run queue</strong>.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"conversion.html\"><span>Previous</span>Conversion</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"ia-video-3d.html\"><span>Next</span>AI for video and 3D</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#ai-generation\">AI Generation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai-magic-eraser\">AI Magic Eraser</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai-cutout\">AI Cutout</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai-enhance\">AI Enhance</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../ia-image.html"}, "ia-video-3d.html": {"title": "AI for video and 3D — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"ai-for-video-and-3d\">AI for video and 3D</h1>\n<h2 id=\"ai-interpolator\">AI Interpolator</h2>\n<p>Makes a video smoother by inventing the missing frames: 30 fps becomes 60, 120 or 240 fps, or a perfect slow\nmotion. Part of <a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium</a>.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/interpolator.jpg\"><img alt=\"The AI Interpolator\" src=\"images/interpolator.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The AI Interpolator</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Source video</strong>: <strong>Browse</strong> or drop a file.</li>\n<li><strong>Output folder</strong>: where to save the result.</li>\n<li><strong>Multiplier</strong>: ×2, ×4, ×8 or <strong>Custom</strong>; then the <strong>Format</strong> and the <strong>Codec</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>GPU</strong>: the card to use; <strong>After</strong>: what Orbit does at the end (nothing, open the folder…).</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Interpolate!</strong>; the <strong>Console</strong> follows each step (extraction, interpolation, rebuild).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The <strong>Presets</strong> tab offers ready settings: <strong>RIFE x2 - Anime-optimized</strong>, RIFE x2 lossless quality, <strong>RIFE x4 -\nSlow-mo x0.5</strong>, <strong>RIFE x4 - 120FPS</strong>, <strong>RIFE x2 → GIF</strong>, <strong>RIFE x8 - 240FPS</strong>. The RIFE engine works with every\nrecent graphics card (Vulkan) and downloads the first time.</p>\n<h2 id=\"topaz-video-ai\">Topaz Video AI</h2>\n<p>Drives <strong>your own</strong> Topaz Video AI install from Orbit, with a queue and a before/after preview. Topaz Video AI\nmust be installed and activated on your PC (Topaz licence). Part of <a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium</a>.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/topaz.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Topaz Video AI tab\" src=\"images/topaz.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Topaz Video AI tab</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Orbit finds Topaz by itself (<strong>Engine detected</strong>); otherwise, <strong>Re-run detection</strong>. The settings follow Topaz's:\n<strong>Enhance &amp; Upscale</strong> (AI model, scale, compression reduction, detail, sharpness, noise, dehalo, grain), frame\ninterpolation (frames per second, slow motion), <strong>Stabilization</strong> (strength, shake, rolling shutter) and\n<strong>Export</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"paint-a-plate\">Paint a plate</h2>\n<p>Retouch a video shot by painting its first frame: erase an object, add one, change the light or add smoke,\nfire, steam. The AI applies the retouch to the whole shot.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/paintaplate.jpg\"><img alt=\"Paint a plate: tools on the left, frame in the middle, history on the right\" src=\"images/paintaplate.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Paint a plate: tools on the left, frame in the middle, history on the right</figcaption></figure>\n<h3 id=\"install\">Install</h3>\n<p>Paint a plate relies on <strong>ComfyUI</strong> and on the open-source <strong>Paint a plate</strong> pack (AInVFX). The tab guides the\ninstall:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>ComfyUI folder</strong>: pick an existing ComfyUI, or <strong>Install ComfyUI</strong> (official portable version, about 2 GB).</li>\n<li><strong>Hugging Face token</strong> (<code>hf_…</code>): some models need one. <strong>Create a token</strong> opens the Hugging Face page; then\n   paste it in the field. It stays on your PC.</li>\n<li><strong>Install what is missing</strong>: the main models (about 61 GB), in the ComfyUI folder. The optional models add\n   <strong>fluid shots</strong> (0.65 GB) and <strong>SDR to HDR</strong> (1.3 GB, licence to accept on Hugging Face).</li>\n<li><strong>Start Paint a plate</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>You need an <strong>NVIDIA</strong> card with 16 GB of video memory for comfortable use. The ComfyUI launch options can limit\nthe memory used (for example <code>--reserve-vram 4 --cache-ram 16</code> on a 16 GB card). The <strong>Stop</strong> button shuts\nComfyUI down and frees the video memory.</p>\n<h3 id=\"retouch-a-shot\">Retouch a shot</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Open a shot: pick the video. Its format, frame rate and frame count show at the top.</li>\n<li>Pick the tool: <strong>Paint</strong> (add or replace), <strong>Erase</strong> (with <strong>Whole object</strong> to select the whole object in one\n   click) or <strong>Light</strong> (relight).</li>\n<li>Paint on the frame, then write the <strong>Description</strong> of the retouch and click <strong>Generate</strong>.</li>\n<li>Compare with <strong>Compare</strong>, play the shot with the bottom bar, then <strong>Export</strong>: the video keeps the source\n   format (codec, frame rate, timecode).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For a <strong>fluid shot</strong> (smoke, steam, fire), paint flat color areas on frame 0 and on the last frame, describe the\nfluid, then <strong>Generate</strong>. The <strong>history</strong>, on the right, keeps every try; <strong>Other seed</strong> runs a variant.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ai-3d-creation\">AI 3D Creation</h2>\n<p>Turns an image into a <strong>textured 3D model</strong>, right on your graphics card (TRELLIS.2 engine). Free tool.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/image3d.jpg\"><img alt=\"AI 3D Creation: settings on the left, 3D preview in the middle\" src=\"images/image3d.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>AI 3D Creation: settings on the left, 3D preview in the middle</figcaption></figure>\n<h3 id=\"install-1\">Install</h3>\n<p>You need an <strong>NVIDIA</strong> card. The first time, click <strong>Install the engine</strong>: Orbit installs Python, PyTorch and the\nlibraries, then the models (several GB). You can keep using Orbit during the install; if it is interrupted, it\nresumes where it stopped.</p>\n<h3 id=\"create-a-model\">Create a model</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Drop an <strong>Image</strong>: one object, clearly visible, on a simple background gives the best results. No image?\n   Describe the object (\"a wooden barrel\") and click <strong>Create the image</strong> (SDXL, locally).</li>\n<li><strong>Extra references</strong> (experimental): other photos of the same object from other angles.</li>\n<li>Set the <strong>Quality</strong> (<strong>Fast</strong>, <strong>High</strong>, <strong>Ultra</strong>) and the number of <strong>Faces</strong>. With less than 20 GB of\n   video memory, the resolution is lowered automatically when needed.</li>\n<li>Options: <strong>Generate the texture</strong> (off = geometry only, much faster), <strong>Remove background</strong>, <strong>Clean remesh</strong>,\n   texture size, steps, seed.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Create the 3D model</strong>. Count one to three minutes depending on the quality.</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"view-improve-export\">View, improve, export</h3>\n<p>The preview turns the model around, with several views: <strong>Texture</strong>, <strong>Clay</strong>, <strong>Mesh</strong>, <strong>Normals</strong>, <strong>UV</strong>.\nThen:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Enhance texture</strong>: adds detail with FLUX.2 klein without changing the colors or the shape (15 GB to download\n  the first time; intensity <strong>Light</strong>, <strong>Medium</strong>, <strong>Strong</strong>);</li>\n<li><strong>Optimize polygons + UVs</strong>: a much lighter mesh that keeps the look;</li>\n<li><strong>Rig</strong>: adds a skeleton with <strong>Rigify</strong> (automatic) or your own <strong>Auto-Rig Pro</strong> (Blender installed\n  required), then <strong>Open the rig in Blender</strong>;</li>\n<li><strong>Export</strong>: GLB, OBJ, STL, PLY, or <strong>Rigged FBX</strong> (skeleton, weights and textures for Unity or Unreal).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All your creations stay in the gallery at the bottom of the screen.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"ia-image.html\"><span>Previous</span>AI for images</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"audio-transcription.html\"><span>Next</span>Audio and transcription</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#ai-interpolator\">AI Interpolator</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#topaz-video-ai\">Topaz Video AI</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#paint-a-plate\">Paint a plate</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai-3d-creation\">AI 3D Creation</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../ia-video-3d.html"}, "audio-transcription.html": {"title": "Audio and transcription — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"audio-and-transcription\">Audio and transcription</h1>\n<h2 id=\"audio-studio\">Audio Studio</h2>\n<p>Processes the audio of a sound file <strong>or of a video</strong>.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/audiostudio.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Audio Studio\" src=\"images/audiostudio.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Audio Studio</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li>Drop your audio files or videos in the area (several at once).</li>\n<li>Select a file and pick the <strong>Processing</strong>:</li>\n</ol>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Processing</th>\n<th>What it does</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Stem separation</strong></td>\n<td>splits vocals from music: <strong>2 stems</strong> (vocals + accompaniment), <strong>4 stems</strong> (vocals, drums, bass, other) or, with Demucs, <strong>6 stems</strong> (+ guitar and piano). <a href=\"premium.html\">Premium</a>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Denoise</strong></td>\n<td>reduces hiss and constant background noise; set the strength.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normalize</strong></td>\n<td>brings the volume to the level of streaming platforms (-14 LUFS, peak -1.5 dBTP).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Extract audio</strong></td>\n<td>takes the sound track out of a video, without re-encoding the picture, as WAV, MP3 or FLAC.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li><strong>Apply to the whole queue</strong> if needed, then <strong>Run queue</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For separation, two engines:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>High quality</strong> (Demucs v4): much better; with an NVIDIA card, it uses the GPU. Install: Demucs + PyTorch GPU\n  (about 2.5 GB) or CPU (about 700 MB). Stems come out as 320 kb/s MP3. <strong>Fast</strong> (about 4 times faster) or <strong>Max\n  quality</strong> (fine-tuned model).</li>\n<li><strong>Fast &amp; light</strong> (Spleeter): fair quality, about 700 MB to install.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"transcription\">Transcription</h2>\n<p>Turns the speech of a video or audio file into text and subtitles, on your computer. Part of\n<a href=\"premium.html\">Orbit Premium</a>.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/transcription.jpg\"><img alt=\"Transcription\" src=\"images/transcription.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Transcription</figcaption></figure>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Choose a video or audio</strong> (MP4, MKV, MOV, MP3, WAV…).</li>\n<li><strong>Language</strong>: <strong>Auto-detect</strong> or the spoken language.</li>\n<li><strong>AI model</strong>: from the fastest (<strong>Base</strong>, about 142 MB) to the most accurate (heavier and slower).</li>\n<li><strong>Export to</strong>: tick the formats you want. Orbit prepares the right file for each program: <strong>Premiere Pro</strong>,\n   <strong>After Effects</strong>, <strong>CapCut</strong>, <strong>DaVinci Resolve</strong>, <strong>Final Cut Pro</strong>, <strong>YouTube / Web</strong>, <strong>Styled\n   subtitles</strong>, <strong>Plain text</strong>, <strong>Data</strong> and <strong>Lyrics</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Burn subtitles into the video</strong> also creates an <code>.mp4</code> with burned-in subtitles (not editable); set the font\n   size and color.</li>\n<li><strong>Output folder</strong> (next to the source file by default), then transcribe and export.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>When it is done, <strong>Open</strong> shows the files created.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"ia-video-3d.html\"><span>Previous</span>AI for video and 3D</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"boite-a-outils.html\"><span>Next</span>Toolbox and media library</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#audio-studio\">Audio Studio</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#transcription\">Transcription</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../audio-transcription.html"}, "boite-a-outils.html": {"title": "Toolbox and media library — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"toolbox-and-media-library\">Toolbox and media library</h1>\n<h2 id=\"toolbox\">Toolbox</h2>\n<p>More than 60 small tools for everyday jobs, each on a single page: pick a tool, drop the file, set two or three\noptions, done.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/toolbox.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Toolbox: search at the top, tools by category\" src=\"images/toolbox.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Toolbox: search at the top, tools by category</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The search bar at the top finds a tool when you type what you want to do (\"gif\", \"compress\", \"audio\"…).</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Category</th>\n<th>Tools</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Video</td>\n<td>Trim, Compress to a size, Crop (social), Rotate / Mirror, Change speed, Reverse, Boomerang, Split into parts, Video → GIF, GIF → MP4, Images → GIF, Watermark / logo, Text watermark, Merge videos, Quick editor, Timeline editor, Slideshow, Screen recorder, Contact sheet, Extract frames, Thumbnail (instant), Convert video, Fade in/out, Denoise / deinterlace, Highlights (auto), Loop video, Replace audio</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Audio</td>\n<td>Extract audio, Normalize / Fade, Cut silences, Merge audio, Voice + music, Audio editor, AI voice studio, Pitch &amp; tempo, Normalize (LUFS), Volume (gain), Audio visualizer, Waveform (image)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Image</td>\n<td>Convert an image, Clean metadata, Rotate / Mirror (image), Crop, Border / frame, Adjustments &amp; filters, Color palette, Apply a LUT, Colorize (AI), YouTube thumbnail, Comparator</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Text and documents</td>\n<td>PDF tools, Burn subtitles, Translate subtitles, QR Code, OCR (text from image)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Files</td>\n<td>Batch rename, Watched folder</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Two tools deserve a word more:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Compress to a size</strong> aims at an exact weight: <strong>Discord (10 MB)</strong>, <strong>E-mail (25 MB)</strong>, <strong>Discord Nitro\n  (50 MB)</strong>, <strong>Nitro+ (500 MB)</strong> or a custom size.</li>\n<li><strong>Watched folder</strong> processes every file that lands in a folder: videos to MP4 (H.264), videos compressed to a\n  target size, videos to MP3, or images to another format. Handy for a captures or exports folder.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"media-library\">Media Library</h2>\n<p>The <strong>Media Library</strong> gathers your videos in a library, with a built-in player.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/library.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Media Library\" src=\"images/library.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Media Library</figcaption></figure>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Add</strong> files, or <strong>Scan</strong> a whole folder (subfolders included).</li>\n<li>On the left: <strong>Whole library</strong>, <strong>Recently added</strong>, <strong>Favorites</strong>, <strong>Resume playback</strong> (started videos resume\n  where you stopped) and <strong>Series</strong> (sorted by season and episode).</li>\n<li>At the top: instant search, <strong>Resolution</strong> and <strong>Codec</strong> filters, sorting by date added, name, duration, size\n  or season/episode.</li>\n<li>Click a video to play it. The <strong>Information</strong> panel shows the codecs, size and duration.</li>\n<li><strong>Creative export</strong>: <strong>Prepare for</strong> a use (editing, social…) picks the right preset, then <strong>Convert</strong>.</li>\n</ul>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"audio-transcription.html\"><span>Previous</span>Audio and transcription</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"drive.html\"><span>Next</span>Discord Drive</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#toolbox\">Toolbox</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#media-library\">Media Library</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../boite-a-outils.html"}, "drive.html": {"title": "Discord Drive — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"discord-drive\">Discord Drive</h1>\n<p>The <strong>Discord Drive</strong> stores your files online by cutting them into <strong>encrypted</strong> pieces (AES-256) sent to\nDiscord. Your files are encrypted on your PC before they leave: neither Discord nor the Orbit server can read\nthem.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Discord is not made to store files and its terms of service do not plan for it: a channel or an account can be\ndeleted. <strong>Always keep another copy of your important files.</strong></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The tab has three modes, at the top right: <strong>Local</strong>, <strong>Cloud (account)</strong> and <strong>Drop</strong>.</p>\n<figure><a href=\"images/drive.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Discord Drive in Local mode, ready to set up\" src=\"images/drive.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Discord Drive in Local mode, ready to set up</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"local-mode\">Local mode</h2>\n<p>Everything stays on your PC (the file list and the key); the pieces go to your own Discord channel.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>On Discord, pick or create a <strong>private channel</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Channel settings › Integrations › Webhooks › New webhook</strong>, then <strong>Copy webhook URL</strong>.</li>\n<li>In Orbit, paste it in <strong>Discord webhook URL</strong>. Several webhooks (one per line, in different channels) make\n   uploads faster.</li>\n<li>Pick a strong <strong>Encryption passphrase</strong>, then <strong>Set up Drive</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Without the passphrase, nobody can read the files back, <strong>not even you</strong>. Write it down somewhere safe: it\ncannot be recovered.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Each time you open it, type the passphrase to <strong>Unlock</strong> the Drive. <strong>Lock</strong> closes it.</p>\n<h2 id=\"cloud-mode-account\">Cloud mode (account)</h2>\n<p>Cloud mode uses an <strong>Orbit account</strong>: your files follow you on all your PCs.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Create account</strong> (e-mail and password) or <strong>Sign in</strong>.</li>\n<li>Pick an <strong>encryption passphrase</strong>; it protects your files and works on all your devices.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Then: <strong>Upload files</strong>, <strong>New folder</strong>, <strong>Refresh</strong>, filter, download, delete. Videos play straight from the\nDrive. <strong>Forgot password?</strong> sends a code by e-mail; it changes the sign-in password, not the passphrase.</p>\n<p>The <strong>Telegram</strong> button stores files on your Telegram account (in your <strong>Saved Messages</strong>) instead of Discord.\nThe Telegram session stays on your PC.</p>\n<h2 id=\"drop-share-without-an-account\">Drop: share without an account</h2>\n<p><strong>Drop</strong> sends a file to someone, even without an account: Orbit encrypts it with a one-time key and gives you a\n<strong>share code</strong>. The other person pastes this code in Drop to download and decrypt the file. Drops expire\nautomatically after a while.</p>\n<p><strong>Shared folders</strong> (codes starting with <code>orbf1_</code>) open in the same place; you can download them, play them or\n<strong>Save to my Drive</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"share-from-the-drive\">Share from the Drive</h2>\n<p>In Cloud mode, <strong>Share</strong> on a file or a folder creates a code: the content is re-encrypted with a new key, your\naccount key is never sent. Give the share a <strong>title</strong>: it is visible to anyone who has the code.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"boite-a-outils.html\"><span>Previous</span>Toolbox and media library</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"reglages.html\"><span>Next</span>Settings</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#local-mode\">Local mode</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#cloud-mode-account\">Cloud mode (account)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#drop-share-without-an-account\">Drop: share without an account</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#share-from-the-drive\">Share from the Drive</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../drive.html"}, "reglages.html": {"title": "Settings — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"settings\">Settings</h1>\n<p>Open the settings with <strong>Settings</strong>, at the bottom of the sidebar. The pages are listed on the left.</p>\n<h2 id=\"general\">General</h2>\n<figure><a href=\"images/settings-general.jpg\"><img alt=\"Settings › General\" src=\"images/settings-general.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Settings › General</figcaption></figure>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Output</strong>: <strong>Download folder</strong>, <strong>Default video format</strong>, <strong>Restricted filenames (ASCII)</strong> (avoids special\n  characters in names).</li>\n<li><strong>Language</strong>: the interface language (English, French, Spanish, German, Italian, Portuguese).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"downloads\">Downloads</h2>\n<figure><a href=\"images/settings-downloads.jpg\"><img alt=\"Settings › Downloads\" src=\"images/settings-downloads.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Settings › Downloads</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Embedded content</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Force H.264 (editing-friendly)</strong>: H.264/AAC for After Effects and Premiere, instead of VP9 or AV1;</li>\n<li><strong>Compress after download</strong>;</li>\n<li><strong>Audio only</strong>: keep only the sound (MP3, FLAC…);</li>\n<li><strong>Embed thumbnail</strong> (cover), <strong>Embed metadata</strong> (title, author, date), <strong>Embed subtitles</strong>, chapters;</li>\n<li>auto-generated subtitles and subtitle languages (comma-separated codes, for example <code>fr.*,en.*</code>);</li>\n<li><strong>Write the .info.json</strong>;</li>\n<li><strong>Mark sponsor segments</strong> (SponsorBlock chapters) or <strong>Remove sponsors</strong> (cuts intro, ads…).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Behavior</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Download archive</strong>: never download again what was already downloaded;</li>\n<li><strong>Ignore errors</strong>: keep going in a playlist when one video fails;</li>\n<li><strong>Keep the original timestamp</strong>, <strong>No .part files</strong>;</li>\n<li><strong>Concurrent fragments</strong>: speeds up HLS and DASH streams;</li>\n<li><strong>Simultaneous AI jobs (GPU)</strong>: how many AI tools use the graphics card at the same time. <strong>1</strong> (a queue) is\n  recommended;</li>\n<li><strong>Maximum VRAM for AI</strong>: a video memory cap for the AI engines, from 1 GB to the size of your card, or\n  <strong>Unlimited</strong>. Useful to keep room for a game or another program;</li>\n<li><strong>Speed limit</strong>: for example <code>5M</code> or <code>800k</code> (empty = unlimited);</li>\n<li><strong>Windows right-click menu</strong>: adds \"Orbit ▸ Compress / Crop…\" to the right-click menu of a file.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Authentication</strong>: <strong>Browser cookies</strong>, for content that needs a login.</p>\n<h2 id=\"appearance\">Appearance</h2>\n<figure><a href=\"images/settings-appearance.jpg\"><img alt=\"Settings › Appearance\" src=\"images/settings-appearance.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Settings › Appearance</figcaption></figure>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Theme</strong>: Nova, Graphite, Black, White, Midnight, or <strong>System</strong> (follows Windows' light/dark mode).</li>\n<li><strong>Setup wizard</strong>: <strong>Relaunch</strong> to rearrange the tabs for your profile.</li>\n<li><strong>Accent color</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Liquid glass (Apple style)</strong>: real refraction on the edge of panels and cards. Presets <strong>Subtle</strong>, <strong>Apple</strong>,\n  <strong>Intense</strong> or <strong>Custom</strong>, then fine settings: refraction, prism effect, glass blur, tint, highlights,\n  mouse-following glare, drop shadow. A live preview shows the result.</li>\n<li><strong>Wallpaper</strong>: an image behind the glass, with its blur and dimming; <strong>Tool page blur</strong> and <strong>Text shadow</strong> keep\n  text readable.</li>\n<li><strong>Brighter text</strong>: lightens the secondary grey texts.</li>\n<li><strong>Reset</strong> puts every glass, background and text setting back to default.</li>\n<li>Interface sounds: small clicks on press.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"ai--performance\">AI &amp; Performance</h2>\n<figure><a href=\"images/settings-ai.jpg\"><img alt=\"Settings › AI &amp; Performance\" src=\"images/settings-ai.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Settings › AI &amp; Performance</figcaption></figure>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>AI Assistant</strong>: <strong>Free local AI</strong> (about 2 GB, downloaded once, works offline) or your <strong>Anthropic API key\n  (Claude)</strong>, more powerful. The key stays on your PC.</li>\n<li><strong>AI Enhance &amp; Topaz</strong>: <strong>Default AI output folder</strong> and <strong>Default GPU</strong> for upscale, interpolation and Topaz.</li>\n<li><strong>Performance</strong>:<ul>\n<li><strong>Disable hardware acceleration</strong> if the interface flickers (restart needed);</li>\n<li><strong>Video encoding</strong> for the Converter: <strong>Auto (GPU if available)</strong>, <strong>NVIDIA GPU (NVENC)</strong> or <strong>Processor\n(CPU)</strong>;</li>\n<li><strong>Max simultaneous downloads</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"modules--ai\">Modules &amp; AI</h2>\n<figure><a href=\"images/settings-modules.jpg\"><img alt=\"Settings › Modules &amp; AI\" src=\"images/settings-modules.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Settings › Modules &amp; AI</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The list of every Orbit engine and model (yt-dlp, ffmpeg, local AI, Real-ESRGAN, RIFE, HandBrake, Magic Eraser,\nCutout, Audio Studio, AI 3D Creation…), with its size and state. Install, update or remove each one in a click;\n<strong>Refresh</strong> checks them all.</p>\n<h2 id=\"network\">Network</h2>\n<figure><a href=\"images/settings-network.jpg\"><img alt=\"Settings › Network\" src=\"images/settings-network.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Settings › Network</figcaption></figure>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Proxy server</strong> and <strong>Test the proxy</strong> (checks the connection through yt-dlp).</li>\n<li><strong>Security</strong>: <strong>Don't verify the HTTPS certificate</strong> (for servers with an invalid certificate; avoid unless\n  needed).</li>\n<li><strong>Advanced</strong>: <strong>Custom yt-dlp arguments</strong>, added to every download.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"system\">System</h2>\n<figure><a href=\"images/settings-system.jpg\"><img alt=\"Settings › System\" src=\"images/settings-system.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Settings › System</figcaption></figure>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Startup &amp; window</strong>: start Orbit with Windows, minimize to the notification area instead of closing,\n  notifications when a download or a render finishes.</li>\n<li><strong>Storage</strong>: <strong>Temporary files</strong> (size of the work files, <strong>Clear</strong> button) and <strong>Orbit data folder</strong>\n  (<strong>Open</strong>).</li>\n<li><strong>Maintenance</strong>: <strong>Re-install yt-dlp</strong> if downloads fail; the JS engine for YouTube (Deno), which avoids the\n  \"no supported JavaScript runtime\" error and missing formats; <strong>View logs</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"about\">About</h2>\n<figure><a href=\"images/settings-about.jpg\"><img alt=\"Settings › About\" src=\"images/settings-about.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Settings › About</figcaption></figure>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Version</strong> and the update check.</li>\n<li>Bug report: describe the problem and send the report. Automatic sending also sends errors on its own (without\n  your files or your user name).</li>\n<li>Privacy: no tracking and no usage statistics; your statistics stay on your device.</li>\n</ul>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"drive.html\"><span>Previous</span>Discord Drive</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"premium.html\"><span>Next</span>Orbit Premium</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#general\">General</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#downloads\">Downloads</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#appearance\">Appearance</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#ai--performance\">AI &amp; Performance</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#modules--ai\">Modules &amp; AI</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#network\">Network</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#system\">System</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#about\">About</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../reglages.html"}, "premium.html": {"title": "Orbit Premium — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"orbit-premium\">Orbit Premium</h1>\n<p>Orbit is free. <strong>Orbit Premium</strong> unlocks the most advanced AI tools, for a <strong>one-time payment of €14.99</strong>, valid\n<strong>for life</strong> on <strong>1 device</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-is-included\">What is included</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Free</th>\n<th>Premium</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Downloads, Spotify, Twitch, file hosts, Subscriptions</td>\n<td>AI Generation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Converter and HandBrake</td>\n<td>AI Magic Eraser</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Toolbox and Media Library</td>\n<td>AI Cutout</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Audio Studio: denoise, normalize, extract</td>\n<td>AI Enhance</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AI 3D Creation</td>\n<td>AI Interpolator</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Paint a plate</td>\n<td>Topaz Video AI</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Discord Drive</td>\n<td>Transcription</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>AI Assistant</td>\n<td>Audio Studio: stem separation</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>A Premium tool stays visible: when opened, it shows a locked screen with the button to go Premium.</p>\n<h2 id=\"buy\">Buy</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Click <strong>Premium</strong> at the bottom of the sidebar (or <strong>Menu › File › Go Premium</strong>).</li>\n<li>Create an account or sign in to your Orbit account.</li>\n<li>Click the buy button (€14.99): payment opens in your browser (Stripe; card, or PayPal depending on your\n   country).</li>\n<li>Come back to Orbit: Premium unlocks by itself as soon as the payment is confirmed.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure><a href=\"images/premium.jpg\"><img alt=\"The Orbit Premium window\" src=\"images/premium.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>The Orbit Premium window</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Paid another way (crypto) or received a key? Use the \"Paid in crypto or received a key?\" link, then activate\nyour key.</p>\n<h2 id=\"gift-premium\">Gift Premium</h2>\n<p>To receive Premium as a gift, with no account or payment: open the Premium window, copy <strong>your device ID</strong> and\ngive it to the person offering it. Once confirmed, click the gift check button: Orbit activates.</p>\n<h2 id=\"good-to-know\">Good to know</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Premium tools run on your PC; once activated, Premium also works offline.</li>\n<li>Premium is tied to one device. To move to another PC, contact support.</li>\n<li>The button at the bottom of the sidebar reads <strong>Premium active</strong> when everything is unlocked.</li>\n</ul>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"reglages.html\"><span>Previous</span>Settings</a>\n<a class=\"next\" href=\"depannage.html\"><span>Next</span>Troubleshooting</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#what-is-included\">What is included</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#buy\">Buy</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#gift-premium\">Gift Premium</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#good-to-know\">Good to know</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../premium.html"}, "depannage.html": {"title": "Troubleshooting — Orbit", "body": "<h1 id=\"troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</h1>\n<h2 id=\"a-download-fails\">A download fails</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Click <strong>Failed — see logs</strong> on the row: the end of the log gives the reason.</li>\n<li>Sites change often: <strong>Settings › System › Re-install yt-dlp</strong> installs the latest version (Orbit also updates\n   it at every launch).</li>\n<li>For YouTube, if the log mentions \"JavaScript runtime\" or formats are missing: <strong>Settings › System</strong>, install\n   the JS engine for YouTube (Deno).</li>\n<li>Private, members-only or age-restricted content: turn on the <strong>Cookie</strong> icon of the bar (you must be signed in\n   to the site in Chrome), or open the page in the <strong>SNIFFER</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Menu › Downloads › Restart Failed Downloads</strong> restarts every failure.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"file-deleted-on-a-finished-download\">\"File deleted\" on a finished download</h2>\n<p>The file was moved or deleted from the disk. <strong>Download again</strong> gets it back, or remove the row.</p>\n<h2 id=\"orbit-closed-during-a-download\">Orbit closed during a download</h2>\n<p>Start Orbit again: downloads resume where they stopped. HandBrake and Topaz queues come back too, but you have\nto restart them by hand.</p>\n<h2 id=\"an-ai-tool-is-slow-or-runs-out-of-memory\">An AI tool is slow or runs out of memory</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Close games and programs that use the graphics card.</li>\n<li>Keep <strong>Settings › Downloads › Simultaneous AI jobs (GPU)</strong> at <strong>1</strong>.</li>\n<li>Set a <strong>Maximum VRAM for AI</strong> to leave some margin.</li>\n<li>In AI Enhance, lower the tile size; in AI 3D Creation, pick <strong>Fast</strong> or fewer <strong>Faces</strong>.</li>\n<li>In Paint a plate, use <strong>Stop</strong> when you are done: ComfyUI frees the video memory.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"an-nvidia-graphics-card-is-required\">\"An NVIDIA graphics card is required\"</h2>\n<p>AI 3D Creation, Paint a plate and local AI Generation use CUDA, which only exists on NVIDIA cards. On another PC,\nAI Generation goes through the online <strong>Flux</strong> service. The other AI tools (upscale, interpolation, cutout, magic\neraser) work with every recent card.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-interface-flickers-or-stays-black\">The interface flickers or stays black</h2>\n<p><strong>Settings › AI &amp; Performance › Disable hardware acceleration</strong>, then restart Orbit. If the interface is slow,\ntone down the <strong>Liquid glass</strong> (<strong>Subtle</strong> preset) or turn it off in <strong>Settings › Appearance</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"a-premium-tool-stays-locked\">A Premium tool stays locked</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Check the bottom of the sidebar: it should read <strong>Premium active</strong>.</li>\n<li>After a payment, open the Premium window: it unlocks as soon as the payment is confirmed.</li>\n<li><strong>Update required</strong>: your version is too old for the AI tools; click the button to install the latest one.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-antivirus-blocks-orbit-or-a-module\">The antivirus blocks Orbit or a module</h2>\n<p>Orbit downloads engines (yt-dlp, ffmpeg, AI models) into <code>C:\\Users\\&lt;you&gt;\\.orbit</code>. If your antivirus blocks one,\nadd this folder to its exceptions, then reinstall the module from <strong>Settings › Modules &amp; AI</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"free-up-space\">Free up space</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Settings › System › Temporary files › Clear</strong> deletes the work files.</li>\n<li><strong>Settings › Modules &amp; AI</strong>: remove the models of tools you do not use (they download again if needed).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"report-a-problem\">Report a problem</h2>\n<p><strong>Settings › About</strong>, bug report: describe what you were doing and what happened, then send the report. The last\n25 lines of the log are attached, without your user name. The full log is in <strong>Settings › System › View logs</strong>.</p>", "pager": "<a class=\"prev\" href=\"premium.html\"><span>Previous</span>Orbit Premium</a>", "toc": "<aside class=\"toc\"><p>On this page</p><ul><li><a href=\"#a-download-fails\">A download fails</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#file-deleted-on-a-finished-download\">\"File deleted\" on a finished download</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#orbit-closed-during-a-download\">Orbit closed during a download</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#an-ai-tool-is-slow-or-runs-out-of-memory\">An AI tool is slow or runs out of memory</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#an-nvidia-graphics-card-is-required\">\"An NVIDIA graphics card is required\"</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#the-interface-flickers-or-stays-black\">The interface flickers or stays black</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#a-premium-tool-stays-locked\">A Premium tool stays locked</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#the-antivirus-blocks-orbit-or-a-module\">The antivirus blocks Orbit or a module</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#free-up-space\">Free up space</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#report-a-problem\">Report a problem</a></li></ul></aside>", "other": "../depannage.html"}};
